x review on PR #484 identified that the shared mutable `sessionIterationMap` approach is fragile — a session-scoped listener pattern would be more robust.\\n\\n**Where**:\\n- `src/cli/commands/ralph.ts` line 1061 — `sessionIterationMap` declaration\\n- `src/cli/commands/ralph.ts` lines 1305-1337 — the `on('update')` handler that uses `sessionIterationMap.get(_sid)` for iteration lookup\\n- `src/cli/commands/ralph.ts` line 1369 — where new sessions are registered in the map\\n\\n**How**:\\nTwo approaches (pick one):\\n\\n1. **Session-scoped listeners** (recommended): Instead of one persistent `on('update')` handler, register a new listener per ACP session that captures the iteration number in its closure. Remove the old listener when the session ends or a new one starts. This eliminates the shared mutable map entirely.\\n\\n2. **Cleanup old sessions**: When starting a new ACP session, remove the previous session's entry from `sessionIterationMap` and call `agent.client.off('update', oldHandler)` to prevent stale callbacks. Less clean but simpler delta.\\n\\nBoth approaches should also ensure the translator is reset between iterations (it already creates a fresh translator per retry, but verify per-iteration reset).\\n\\n**Done when**:\\n- Late updates from a previous ACP session are attributed to the correct iteration (the one that created that session)\\n- No shared mutable state for iteration tracking — either session-scoped closures or explicit cleanup\\n- Existing event logging tests still pass\\n- Event log entries show correct iteration numbers even when sessions overlap\",\n      \"status\": \"pending_review\",\n      \"started_at\": \"2026-02-28T23:27:38.188Z\",\n      \"priority\": 3,\n      \"spec_ref\": \"@cli-ralph\",\n      \"note_count\": 6,\n      \"last_note_at\": \"2026-02-28T23:27:53.779Z\",\n      \"todo_count\": 0,\n      \"incomplete_todos\": 0\n    }\n  ],\n  \"recent_notes\": [\n    {\n      \"task_ref\": \"01KJDQ1A\",\n      \"task_title\": \"Ralph event handler iteration attribution should use session-scoped mapping instead of shared mutabl\",\n      \"task_status\": \"pending_review\",\n      \"note_ulid\": \"01KJK98X\",\n      \"created_at\": \"2026-02-28T23:27:53.779Z\",\n      \"author\": \"@claude\",\n      \"content\": \"[FIX_CYCLE: 2] Pushed commit 3eba7201 to PR #612 with listener detach on rotation/end/dispose and regression test coverage for replaceSessionUpdateLogger ordering.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"task_ref\": \"01KJDQ1A\",\n      \"task_title\": \"Ralph event handler iteration attribution should use session-scoped mapping instead of shared mutabl\",\n      \"task_status\": \"pending_review\",\n      \"note_ulid\": \"01KJK98J\",\n      \"created_at\": \"2026-02-28T23:27:41.786Z\",\n      \"author\": \"@claude\",\n      \"content\": \"[FIX_CYCLE: 2] Addressed PR #612 MUST-FIX listener accumulation by tracking one active session.update logger and detaching it via replaceSessionUpdateLogger() on session rotation, error cleanup, periodic restart, and final cleanup. Added unit regression test for detach-then-attach behavior in tests/ralph.test.ts. Verification: npm test -- tests/ralph.test.ts (142 passed). kspec validate still reports pre-existing meta/reference issues unrelated to this task (@observations ambiguity, missing observations skill file).\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"task_ref\": \"01KJDQ1A\",\n      \"task_title\": \"Ralph event handler iteration attribution should use session-scoped mapping instead of shared mutabl\",\n      \"task_status\": \"pending_review\",\n      \"note_ulid\": \"01KJK94B\",\n      \"created_at\": \"2026-02-28T23:25:23.674Z\",\n      \"author\": \"@claude\",\n      \"content\": \"[FIX_CYCLE: 1] Review findings: MUST-FIX: PR #612 adds a new update listener per iteration without removing prior listeners; listener accumulation risks memory leaks and EventEmitter warnings over long ralph loops.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"task_ref\": \"01KJDQ1A\",\n      \"task_title\": \"Ralph event handler iteration attribution should use session-scoped mapping instead of shared mutabl\",\n      \"task_status\": \"pending_review\",\n      \"note_ulid\": \"01KJK8RV\",\n      \"created_at\": \"2026-02-28T23:19:07.489Z\",\n      \"author\": \"@claude\",\n      \"content\": \"Implemented session-scoped streaming update attribution for Ralph iterations.\\n- Replaced shared mutable sessionIterationMap approach with createSessionUpdateLogger(acpSessionId, iteration, logUpdate).\\n- Each ACP session now registers a logger that captures iteration in closure and ignores updates from other session IDs.\\n- Logging callback now safely swallows both sync and async logging failures.\\n- Updated helper tests in tests/ralph.test.ts to cover session-bound attribution and logger error swallowing.\\nVerification: npm test -- tests/ralph.test.ts (141 passed).\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"task_ref\": \"01KJDQ17W\",\n      \"task_title\": \"Ralph loop needs iteration-level timeout. When a spawned agent gets stuck (e.g., tool call hanging o\",\n      \"task_status\": \"completed\",\n      \"note_ulid\": \"01KJK83G\",\n      \"created_at\": \"2026-02-28T23:07:27.825Z\",\n      \"author\": \"@claude\",\n      \"content\": \"FIX_CYCLE: 6 Inherited needs_work task and verified PR #610 currently has no review comments/threads and all checks passing. Transitioned task through in_progress and re-submitted to pending_review for external review/merge.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"task_ref\": \"01KJDQ1B\",\n      \"task_title\": \"Plan import warnings treated as errors in batch mode. The no YAML code block in specs section warnin\",\n      \"task_status\": \"completed\",\n      \"note_ulid\": \"01KJK81Q\",\n      \"created_at\": \"2026-02-28T23:06:29.741Z\",\n      \"author\": \"@claude\",\n      \"content\": \"[RALPH SUBAGENT] Subagent timed out after 20 minutes\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"task_ref\": \"01KJDQ1B\",\n      \"task_title\": \"Plan import warnings treated as errors in batch mode. The no YAML code block in specs section warnin\",\n      \"task_status\": \"completed\",\n      \"note_ulid\": \"01KJK81N\",\n      \"created_at\": \"2026-02-28T23:06:26.776Z\",\n      \"author\": \"@claude\",\n      \"content\": \"Automation status set to needs_review: Subagent timed out after 20 minutes\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"task_ref\": \"01KJDQ17W\",\n      \"task_title\": \"Ralph loop needs iteration-level timeout. When a spawned agent gets stuck (e.g., tool call hanging o\",\n      \"task_status\": \"completed\",\n      \"note_ulid\": \"01KJK7AY\",\n      \"created_at\": \"2026-02-28T22:54:03.228Z\",\n      \"author\": \"@claude\",\n      \"content\": \"FIX_CYCLE: 5 complete. Opened PR #610 (https://github.com/kynetic-ai/kynetic-spec/pull/610) with:\\n1. Fixed floating runIterationPrompts() promise (.catch(() => {}) before Promise.race)\\n2. Added @cli-ralph ac-24/ac-25/ac-26 for --iteration-timeout feature\\n3. Added // AC: annotations to tests/ralph.test.ts\\nAll 140 ralph tests pass.\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"active_todos\": [],\n  \"ready_tasks\": [\n    {\n      \"ref\": \"01KJGDR9\",\n      \"slug\": null,\n      \"title\": \"Fix ralph session-budget-integration test timeouts\",\n      \"description\": \"2 tests failing in tests/ralph/session-budget-integration.test.ts: (1) ralph loop times out waiting for completion marker, (2) output doesn't contain expected 'Iteration failed' string. These are race conditions or mock issues in the ralph loop test harness, not version bump related. Originally bundled in @01KJDSXEME66TYKVVGGFW6PYT2 which was cancelled after the version-bump failures resolved themselves.\",\n      \"priority\": 1,\n      \"spec_ref\": null,\n      \"tags\": [\n        \"bug\",\n        \"testing\",\n        \"ralph\"\n      ],\n      \"unlocks\": 0\n    },\n    {\n      \"ref\": \"01KHF2BK\",\n      \"slug\": null,\n      \"title\": \"Revisit ralph wrap-up agent design and test coverage\",\n      \"description\": \"PR #369 added a wrap-up agent that runs on ralph loop exit. Retrospective flagged it as over-engineered but the intent is broader than simple cleanup: it ensures all work is completed, finds in-progress work where task state doesn't match reality, root-causes whether work is still needed, and does best-effort to get the project into a clean state (either continue the loop or put work on a branch with a task for the user). Too many possible states to rely on code alone — the agent approach is intentional. However: runWrapUpAgent() has zero integration tests (all 37 tests only check prompt strings and boolean helpers). Revisit AC coverage, add integration tests for the actual agent spawn/timeout/cleanup paths, and verify the prompt adequately covers the intended scenarios.\",\n      \"priority\": 2,\n      \"spec_ref\": null,\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"unlocks\": 0\n    },\n    {\n      \"ref\": \"01KHF2BN\",\n      \"slug\": null,\n      \"title\": \"Create spec for validate --drift feature\",\n      \"description\": \"PR #362 added kspec validate --drift, a user-facing CLI flag for AC schema field validation. This was shipped without a spec item or formal ACs, violating the spec-before-code rule. Create a spec item with acceptance criteria covering: field detection from prose, conceptual vs schema fields, strict mode, exit codes, and false positive handling.\",\n      \"priority\": 2,\n      \"spec_ref\": null,\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"unlocks\": 0\n    },\n    {\n      \"ref\": \"01KHF34K\",\n      \"slug\": null,\n      \"title\": \"Add code-level reflect gating in ralph based on iteration delta\",\n      \"description\": \"PR #357 added skill-file instructions to gate reflection on meaningful work, but this has no enforcement. Instead: ralph should snapshot session state (task statuses, working tree, commit count) before each iteration, compare at the end, and only issue the reflect prompt if something measurably changed (task transitions, commits, file changes). The reflect prompt itself was already efficient at avoiding noisy observations — the issue is invoking it at all when nothing happened.\",\n      \"priority\": 2,\n      \"spec_ref\": null,\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"unlocks\": 0\n    },\n    {\n      \"ref\": \"01KHVMWP\",\n      \"slug\": null,\n      \"title\": \"Write getting-started tutorial and README for external users\",\n      \"description\": \"kspec has no end-to-end tutorial for new users. INSTALL.md covers setup mechanics but doesn't show the workflow. README.md is either missing or developer-focused on the kspec project itself, not on using kspec as a tool.\\n\\n## What's needed\\n\\n**README.md** — Public-facing, explains:\\n- What kspec is (spec-first task management for AI-assisted development)\\n- Why (shadow branch, spec-driven workflow, agent integration)\\n- Quick install and init\\n- Link to getting-started tutorial\\n\\n**Getting-started tutorial** (docs/getting-started.md or similar):\\n- Walk through from 'npm install -g' to first completed task\\n- Create a spec item with acceptance criteria\\n- Derive a task from the spec\\n- Work the task (start, implement, note, submit)\\n- Create a PR with kspec trailers\\n- Complete the task\\n- Show the spec-first loop in action\\n\\n**Reference points:**\\n- kynetic-bot, imgen, comfy-ecaj-nodes are real consumer projects showing actual usage patterns\\n- All three independently converged on the same Quick Start: kspec init → kspec setup → kspec session start\\n- The workflow skills (task-work, pr, spec) contain detailed command references that the tutorial can link to rather than duplicate\\n- INSTALL.md already covers setup mechanics — tutorial should reference it, not repeat it\\n\\n## Scope boundaries\\n- README is for the npm package / GitHub repo landing page\\n- Tutorial is for humans AND agents onboarding to a new kspec project\\n- Don't duplicate skill content — link to skills for detailed command syntax\\n- Keep it practical with real examples, not abstract descriptions\",\n      \"priority\": 2,\n      \"spec_ref\": null,\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"unlocks\": 0\n    }\n  ],\n  \"blocked_tasks\": [],\n  \"recently_completed\": [\n    {\n      \"ref\": \"01KJDQ17W\",\n      \"slug\": null,\n      \"title\": \"Ralph loop needs iteration-level timeout. When a spawned agent gets stuck (e.g., tool call hanging o\",\n      \"completed_at\": \"2026-02-28T23:14:18.000Z\",\n      \"closed_reason\": \"Merged in PR #610. Implemented iteration-timeout hardening by capturing runIterationPrompts() promise and attaching catch before Promise.race to prevent Node.js 22 unhandled rejection on timeout/dispose path. Added/confirmed @cli-ralph ac-24/ac-25/ac-26 for iteration-timeout defaults, validation, and iteration.timeout event behavior, with AC annotations in tests/ralph.test.ts. Verified @cli-ralph AC annotation coverage across ac-1..ac-26 and green PR CI on merge commit 3935ca808c131813871ec5a48e7550f9a239a5a1.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"ref\": \"01KJDQ1B\",\n      \"slug\": null,\n      \"title\": \"Plan import warnings treated as errors in batch mode. The no YAML code block in specs section warnin\",\n      \"completed_at\": \"2026-02-28T23:05:33.314Z\",\n      \"closed_reason\": \"Merged in PR #609. Fixed batch-mode plan import by replacing process.exit(EXIT_CODES.SUCCESS) with return in plan-import.ts success path, preventing BatchExitError interception. Added regression test in batch-exec-engine.test.ts covering warning-only plan import succeeds in batch (ac-34, ac-23). All CI checks passed.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"ref\": \"01KJGBWP\",\n      \"slug\": \"implement-auto-abandon-metadata-and-audit-trail\",\n      \"title\": \"Implement Auto-abandon Metadata and Audit Trail\",\n      \"completed_at\": \"2026-02-28T22:19:13.639Z\",\n      \"closed_reason\": \"Merged in PR #607. Implemented stale auto-abandon metadata apply helper with canonical close_reason format, shared ended_at/status=abandoned updates, dry-run preview, and one command-specific shadow commit path for multi-session persistence. Verified AC coverage for @session-stale-close-metadata ac-1..ac-4 in tests/session-stale-criteria.test.ts and confirmed green CI on commit 8131a376.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"ref\": \"01KJGBWNW\",\n      \"slug\": \"implement-stale-session-candidate-criteria\",\n      \"title\": \"Implement Stale Session Candidate Criteria\",\n      \"completed_at\": \"2026-02-28T21:43:37.853Z\",\n      \"closed_reason\": \"Merged in PR #605. Implemented stale session candidate criteria engine with relative-duration validation/defaults, AND threshold evaluation, started_at fallback, strict corrupt/unreadable events handling with skipped/failure reporting, and liveness guard suppression. AC coverage verified for @session-stale-criteria ac-1 through ac-8 (including unreadable events path).\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"ref\": \"01KJGQVK\",\n      \"slug\": null,\n      \"title\": \"Clarify core skill update behavior for local template edits\",\n      \"completed_at\": \"2026-02-28T20:58:20.117Z\",\n      \"closed_reason\": \"Merged in PR #603. Implemented same-version template drift detection in skill update and explicit guidance to run 'kspec skill install-core' when local files differ despite matching version, including dry-run output. Added regression tests for drift guidance in tests/core-skill-update.test.ts. AC coverage confirmed for @core-skill-update ac-1, ac-2, ac-3; full regression suite passed via npm test.\",\n      \"origin\": \"observation_promotion\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"ref\": \"01KJGV65\",\n      \"slug\": null,\n      \"title\": \"Add integration test for config-aware init output messaging\",\n      \"completed_at\": \"2026-02-28T20:51:34.652Z\",\n      \"closed_reason\": \"Merged in PR #604. Added integration test coverage in tests/init-setup-integration.test.ts for config-aware init output messaging when running without --setup; verifies custom shadow directory (.specs) and branch (specs-meta) are shown in Next steps/Note output and guards against fallback to hardcoded defaults. AC coverage confirmed for @init-setup-integration ac-1 through ac-4 (trait ACs N/A).\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"ref\": \"01KJHAD8\",\n      \"slug\": null,\n      \"title\": \"Fix: Truncate oversized ACP prompt payloads\",\n      \"completed_at\": \"2026-02-28T19:01:41.319Z\",\n      \"closed_reason\": \"PR #590 reviewed and merged at head 690d0648\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"ref\": \"01KJJGJ1\",\n      \"slug\": null,\n      \"title\": \"Fix merge driver non-interactive flag and improve conflict resolution\",\n      \"completed_at\": \"2026-02-28T16:58:33.763Z\",\n      \"closed_reason\": \"Merged in PR #601. Fixed merge driver: (1) shadow.ts validates/fixes stale config missing --non-interactive, (2) TTY detection auto-enables non-interactive when stdin is not TTY, (3) non-interactive mode exits 0 even with conflicts per spec ac-10. All tests pass.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"ref\": \"01KJDQ19\",\n      \"slug\": null,\n      \"title\": \"CLI args should accept both kebab-case and underscore variants (e.g. depends-on and depends_on). Cur\",\n      \"completed_at\": \"2026-02-28T14:07:12.388Z\",\n      \"closed_reason\": \"Merged in PR #600. Implemented canonical arg-key normalization for batch args so kebab-case, camelCase, and underscore variants are accepted consistently in validation, required-arg checks, and argv generation. Added underscore regression tests in batch schema and batch exec engine coverage. Verified by full npm test (3550 passed) and green PR CI checks on commit b7b44fb4a11a5a4d655333b96a9e13368d95b9ed.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"ref\": \"01KJDQ11\",\n      \"slug\": null,\n      \"title\": \"Fix @observations slug ambiguity — kspec validate reports 6 errors for duplicate slug. Pre-existing \",\n      \"completed_at\": \"2026-02-28T13:53:13.698Z\",\n      \"closed_reason\": \"Merged in PR #599 (commit 5ee2254244a7c9aa718493418964a600869f4b97). Removed legacy /kspec:observations skill entry ambiguity by retaining canonical /kspec:observe in generated agent instructions; duplicate @observations reference errors resolved (References: OK). AC coverage N/A for this infra task (no spec_ref). Local regression: npm test passed (3548 passed, 0 failed).\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"recent_commits\": [\n    {\n      \"hash\": \"3eba720\",\n      \"full_hash\": \"3eba7201e29fc38355da7c3eb8b78be74888ad88\",\n      \"date\": \"2026-02-28T23:27:46.000Z\",\n      \"message\": \"fix: detach ralph session update listeners between iterations\",\n      \"author\": \"Jacob Chapel\",\n      \"task_refs\": [\n        \"01KJDQ1A\"\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"hash\": \"4c81ac5\",\n      \"full_hash\": \"4c81ac594ebc432e3e7114e003b0c374a5464704\",\n      \"date\": \"2026-02-28T23:19:12.000Z\",\n      \"message\": \"fix: use session-scoped ralph update attribution\",\n      \"author\": \"Jacob Chapel\",\n      \"task_refs\": [\n        \"01KJDQ1AF125H0FK29HE769R4P\"\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"hash\": \"3935ca8\",\n      \"full_hash\": \"3935ca808c131813871ec5a48e7550f9a239a5a1\",\n      \"date\": \"2026-02-28T23:14:04.000Z\",\n      \"message\": \"fix: prevent unhandled rejection on iteration timeout (Node.js 22) (#610)\",\n      \"author\": \"Jacob Chapel\",\n      \"task_refs\": [\n        \"01KJDQ17W\"\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":4,"nanos":915525232},"formatted_output":"ℹ Synced shadow branch from remote\n{\n  \"generated_at\": \"2026-02-28T23:28:16.778Z\",\n  \"branch\": \"fix/ralph-session-update-attribution\",\n  \"context\": {\n    \"focus\": null,\n    \"threads\": [],\n    \"open_questions\": [],\n    \"updated_at\": \"2026-01-22T21:05:45.847Z\"\n  },\n  \"active_tasks\": [],\n  \"pending_review_tasks\": [\n    {\n      \"ref\": \"01KJDQ1A\",\n      \"slug\": null,\n      \"title\": \"Ralph event handler iteration attribution should use session-scoped mapping instead of shared mutabl\",\n      \"description\": \"**What**: Ralph event handler uses a `sessionIterationMap` (Map<string, number>) to attribute late ACP session updates to the correct iteration. However, the current implementation has a race condition: when a new ACP session starts for iteration N+1, late updates from iteration N's session can arrive after `sessionIterationMap.set(newSessionId, N+1)` but the old session's listener may still fire. The `_sid` closure variable in the `on('update')` handler captures the session ID correctly, but there is no cleanup of old listeners when starting a new session.\\n\\nThe Codex review on PR #484 identified that the shared mutable `sessionIterationMap` approach is fragile — a session-scoped listener pattern would be more robust.\\n\\n**Where**:\\n- `src/cli/commands/ralph.ts` line 1061 — `sessionIterationMap` declaration\\n- `src/cli/commands/ralph.ts` lines 1305-1337 — the `on('update')` handler that uses `sessionIterationMap.get(_sid)` for iteration lookup\\n- `src/cli/commands/ralph.ts` line 1369 — where new sessions are registered in the map\\n\\n**How**:\\nTwo approaches (pick one):\\n\\n1. **Session-scoped listeners** (recommended): Instead of one persistent `on('update')` handler, register a new listener per ACP session that captures the iteration number in its closure. Remove the old listener when the session ends or a new one starts. This eliminates the shared mutable map entirely.\\n\\n2. **Cleanup old sessions**: When starting a new ACP session, remove the previous session's entry from `sessionIterationMap` and call `agent.client.off('update', oldHandler)` to prevent stale callbacks. Less clean but simpler delta.\\n\\nBoth approaches should also ensure the translator is reset between iterations (it already creates a fresh translator per retry, but verify per-iteration reset).\\n\\n**Done when**:\\n- Late updates from a previous ACP session are attributed to the correct iteration (the one that created that session)\\n- No shared mutable state for iteration tracking — either session-scoped closures or explicit cleanup\\n- Existing event logging tests still pass\\n- Event log entries show correct iteration numbers even when sessions overlap\",\n      \"status\": \"pending_review\",\n      \"started_at\": \"2026-02-28T23:27:38.188Z\",\n      \"priority\": 3,\n      \"spec_ref\": \"@cli-ralph\",\n      \"note_count\": 6,\n      \"last_note_at\": \"2026-02-28T23:27:53.779Z\",\n      \"todo_count\": 0,\n      \"incomplete_todos\": 0\n    }\n  ],\n  \"recent_notes\": [\n    {\n      \"task_ref\": \"01KJDQ1A\",\n      \"task_title\": \"Ralph event handler iteration attribution should use session-scoped mapping instead of shared mutabl\",\n      \"task_status\": \"pending_review\",\n      \"note_ulid\": \"01KJK98X\",\n      \"created_at\": \"2026-02-28T23:27:53.779Z\",\n      \"author\": \"@claude\",\n      \"content\": \"[FIX_CYCLE: 2] Pushed commit 3eba7201 to PR #612 with listener detach on rotation/end/dispose and regression test coverage for replaceSessionUpdateLogger ordering.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"task_ref\": \"01KJDQ1A\",\n      \"task_title\": \"Ralph event handler iteration attribution should use session-scoped mapping instead of shared mutabl\",\n      \"task_status\": \"pending_review\",\n      \"note_ulid\": \"01KJK98J\",\n      \"created_at\": \"2026-02-28T23:27:41.786Z\",\n      \"author\": \"@claude\",\n      \"content\": \"[FIX_CYCLE: 2] Addressed PR #612 MUST-FIX listener accumulation by tracking one active session.update logger and detaching it via replaceSessionUpdateLogger() on session rotation, error cleanup, periodic restart, and final cleanup. Added unit regression test for detach-then-attach behavior in tests/ralph.test.ts. Verification: npm test -- tests/ralph.test.ts (142 passed). kspec validate still reports pre-existing meta/reference issues unrelated to this task (@observations ambiguity, missing observations skill file).\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"task_ref\": \"01KJDQ1A\",\n      \"task_title\": \"Ralph event handler iteration attribution should use session-scoped mapping instead of shared mutabl\",\n      \"task_status\": \"pending_review\",\n      \"note_ulid\": \"01KJK94B\",\n      \"created_at\": \"2026-02-28T23:25:23.674Z\",\n      \"author\": \"@claude\",\n      \"content\": \"[FIX_CYCLE: 1] Review findings: MUST-FIX: PR #612 adds a new update listener per iteration without removing prior listeners; listener accumulation risks memory leaks and EventEmitter warnings over long ralph loops.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"task_ref\": \"01KJDQ1A\",\n      \"task_title\": \"Ralph event handler iteration attribution should use session-scoped mapping instead of shared mutabl\",\n      \"task_status\": \"pending_review\",\n      \"note_ulid\": \"01KJK8RV\",\n      \"created_at\": \"2026-02-28T23:19:07.489Z\",\n      \"author\": \"@claude\",\n      \"content\": \"Implemented session-scoped streaming update attribution for Ralph iterations.\\n- Replaced shared mutable sessionIterationMap approach with createSessionUpdateLogger(acpSessionId, iteration, logUpdate).\\n- Each ACP session now registers a logger that captures iteration in closure and ignores updates from other session IDs.\\n- Logging callback now safely swallows both sync and async logging failures.\\n- Updated helper tests in tests/ralph.test.ts to cover session-bound attribution and logger error swallowing.\\nVerification: npm test -- tests/ralph.test.ts (141 passed).\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"task_ref\": \"01KJDQ17W\",\n      \"task_title\": \"Ralph loop needs iteration-level timeout. When a spawned agent gets stuck (e.g., tool call hanging o\",\n      \"task_status\": \"completed\",\n      \"note_ulid\": \"01KJK83G\",\n      \"created_at\": \"2026-02-28T23:07:27.825Z\",\n      \"author\": \"@claude\",\n      \"content\": \"FIX_CYCLE: 6 Inherited needs_work task and verified PR #610 currently has no review comments/threads and all checks passing. Transitioned task through in_progress and re-submitted to pending_review for external review/merge.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"task_ref\": \"01KJDQ1B\",\n      \"task_title\": \"Plan import warnings treated as errors in batch mode. The no YAML code block in specs section warnin\",\n      \"task_status\": \"completed\",\n      \"note_ulid\": \"01KJK81Q\",\n      \"created_at\": \"2026-02-28T23:06:29.741Z\",\n      \"author\": \"@claude\",\n      \"content\": \"[RALPH SUBAGENT] Subagent timed out after 20 minutes\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"task_ref\": \"01KJDQ1B\",\n      \"task_title\": \"Plan import warnings treated as errors in batch mode. The no YAML code block in specs section warnin\",\n      \"task_status\": \"completed\",\n      \"note_ulid\": \"01KJK81N\",\n      \"created_at\": \"2026-02-28T23:06:26.776Z\",\n      \"author\": \"@claude\",\n      \"content\": \"Automation status set to needs_review: Subagent timed out after 20 minutes\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"task_ref\": \"01KJDQ17W\",\n      \"task_title\": \"Ralph loop needs iteration-level timeout. When a spawned agent gets stuck (e.g., tool call hanging o\",\n      \"task_status\": \"completed\",\n      \"note_ulid\": \"01KJK7AY\",\n      \"created_at\": \"2026-02-28T22:54:03.228Z\",\n      \"author\": \"@claude\",\n      \"content\": \"FIX_CYCLE: 5 complete. Opened PR #610 (https://github.com/kynetic-ai/kynetic-spec/pull/610) with:\\n1. Fixed floating runIterationPrompts() promise (.catch(() => {}) before Promise.race)\\n2. Added @cli-ralph ac-24/ac-25/ac-26 for --iteration-timeout feature\\n3. Added // AC: annotations to tests/ralph.test.ts\\nAll 140 ralph tests pass.\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"active_todos\": [],\n  \"ready_tasks\": [\n    {\n      \"ref\": \"01KJGDR9\",\n      \"slug\": null,\n      \"title\": \"Fix ralph session-budget-integration test timeouts\",\n      \"description\": \"2 tests failing in tests/ralph/session-budget-integration.test.ts: (1) ralph loop times out waiting for completion marker, (2) output doesn't contain expected 'Iteration failed' string. These are race conditions or mock issues in the ralph loop test harness, not version bump related. Originally bundled in @01KJDSXEME66TYKVVGGFW6PYT2 which was cancelled after the version-bump failures resolved themselves.\",\n      \"priority\": 1,\n      \"spec_ref\": null,\n      \"tags\": [\n        \"bug\",\n        \"testing\",\n        \"ralph\"\n      ],\n      \"unlocks\": 0\n    },\n    {\n      \"ref\": \"01KHF2BK\",\n      \"slug\": null,\n      \"title\": \"Revisit ralph wrap-up agent design and test coverage\",\n      \"description\": \"PR #369 added a wrap-up agent that runs on ralph loop exit. Retrospective flagged it as over-engineered but the intent is broader than simple cleanup: it ensures all work is completed, finds in-progress work where task state doesn't match reality, root-causes whether work is still needed, and does best-effort to get the project into a clean state (either continue the loop or put work on a branch with a task for the user). Too many possible states to rely on code alone — the agent approach is intentional. However: runWrapUpAgent() has zero integration tests (all 37 tests only check prompt strings and boolean helpers). Revisit AC coverage, add integration tests for the actual agent spawn/timeout/cleanup paths, and verify the prompt adequately covers the intended scenarios.\",\n      \"priority\": 2,\n      \"spec_ref\": null,\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"unlocks\": 0\n    },\n    {\n      \"ref\": \"01KHF2BN\",\n      \"slug\": null,\n      \"title\": \"Create spec for validate --drift feature\",\n      \"description\": \"PR #362 added kspec validate --drift, a user-facing CLI flag for AC schema field validation. This was shipped without a spec item or formal ACs, violating the spec-before-code rule. Create a spec item with acceptance criteria covering: field detection from prose, conceptual vs schema fields, strict mode, exit codes, and false positive handling.\",\n      \"priority\": 2,\n      \"spec_ref\": null,\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"unlocks\": 0\n    },\n    {\n      \"ref\": \"01KHF34K\",\n      \"slug\": null,\n      \"title\": \"Add code-level reflect gating in ralph based on iteration delta\",\n      \"description\": \"PR #357 added skill-file instructions to gate reflection on meaningful work, but this has no enforcement. Instead: ralph should snapshot session state (task statuses, working tree, commit count) before each iteration, compare at the end, and only issue the reflect prompt if something measurably changed (task transitions, commits, file changes). The reflect prompt itself was already efficient at avoiding noisy observations — the issue is invoking it at all when nothing happened.\",\n      \"priority\": 2,\n      \"spec_ref\": null,\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"unlocks\": 0\n    },\n    {\n      \"ref\": \"01KHVMWP\",\n      \"slug\": null,\n      \"title\": \"Write getting-started tutorial and README for external users\",\n      \"description\": \"kspec has no end-to-end tutorial for new users. INSTALL.md covers setup mechanics but doesn't show the workflow. README.md is either missing or developer-focused on the kspec project itself, not on using kspec as a tool.\\n\\n## What's needed\\n\\n**README.md** — Public-facing, explains:\\n- What kspec is (spec-first task management for AI-assisted development)\\n- Why (shadow branch, spec-driven workflow, agent integration)\\n- Quick install and init\\n- Link to getting-started tutorial\\n\\n**Getting-started tutorial** (docs/getting-started.md or similar):\\n- Walk through from 'npm install -g' to first completed task\\n- Create a spec item with acceptance criteria\\n- Derive a task from the spec\\n- Work the task (start, implement, note, submit)\\n- Create a PR with kspec trailers\\n- Complete the task\\n- Show the spec-first loop in action\\n\\n**Reference points:**\\n- kynetic-bot, imgen, comfy-ecaj-nodes are real consumer projects showing actual usage patterns\\n- All three independently converged on the same Quick Start: kspec init → kspec setup → kspec session start\\n- The workflow skills (task-work, pr, spec) contain detailed command references that the tutorial can link to rather than duplicate\\n- INSTALL.md already covers setup mechanics — tutorial should reference it, not repeat it\\n\\n## Scope boundaries\\n- README is for the npm package / GitHub repo landing page\\n- Tutorial is for humans AND agents onboarding to a new kspec project\\n- Don't duplicate skill content — link to skills for detailed command syntax\\n- Keep it practical with real examples, not abstract descriptions\",\n      \"priority\": 2,\n      \"spec_ref\": null,\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"unlocks\": 0\n    }\n  ],\n  \"blocked_tasks\": [],\n  \"recently_completed\": [\n    {\n      \"ref\": \"01KJDQ17W\",\n      \"slug\": null,\n      \"title\": \"Ralph loop needs iteration-level timeout. When a spawned agent gets stuck (e.g., tool call hanging o\",\n      \"completed_at\": \"2026-02-28T23:14:18.000Z\",\n      \"closed_reason\": \"Merged in PR #610. Implemented iteration-timeout hardening by capturing runIterationPrompts() promise and attaching catch before Promise.race to prevent Node.js 22 unhandled rejection on timeout/dispose path. Added/confirmed @cli-ralph ac-24/ac-25/ac-26 for iteration-timeout defaults, validation, and iteration.timeout event behavior, with AC annotations in tests/ralph.test.ts. Verified @cli-ralph AC annotation coverage across ac-1..ac-26 and green PR CI on merge commit 3935ca808c131813871ec5a48e7550f9a239a5a1.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"ref\": \"01KJDQ1B\",\n      \"slug\": null,\n      \"title\": \"Plan import warnings treated as errors in batch mode. The no YAML code block in specs section warnin\",\n      \"completed_at\": \"2026-02-28T23:05:33.314Z\",\n      \"closed_reason\": \"Merged in PR #609. Fixed batch-mode plan import by replacing process.exit(EXIT_CODES.SUCCESS) with return in plan-import.ts success path, preventing BatchExitError interception. Added regression test in batch-exec-engine.test.ts covering warning-only plan import succeeds in batch (ac-34, ac-23). All CI checks passed.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"ref\": \"01KJGBWP\",\n      \"slug\": \"implement-auto-abandon-metadata-and-audit-trail\",\n      \"title\": \"Implement Auto-abandon Metadata and Audit Trail\",\n      \"completed_at\": \"2026-02-28T22:19:13.639Z\",\n      \"closed_reason\": \"Merged in PR #607. Implemented stale auto-abandon metadata apply helper with canonical close_reason format, shared ended_at/status=abandoned updates, dry-run preview, and one command-specific shadow commit path for multi-session persistence. Verified AC coverage for @session-stale-close-metadata ac-1..ac-4 in tests/session-stale-criteria.test.ts and confirmed green CI on commit 8131a376.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"ref\": \"01KJGBWNW\",\n      \"slug\": \"implement-stale-session-candidate-criteria\",\n      \"title\": \"Implement Stale Session Candidate Criteria\",\n      \"completed_at\": \"2026-02-28T21:43:37.853Z\",\n      \"closed_reason\": \"Merged in PR #605. Implemented stale session candidate criteria engine with relative-duration validation/defaults, AND threshold evaluation, started_at fallback, strict corrupt/unreadable events handling with skipped/failure reporting, and liveness guard suppression. AC coverage verified for @session-stale-criteria ac-1 through ac-8 (including unreadable events path).\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"ref\": \"01KJGQVK\",\n      \"slug\": null,\n      \"title\": \"Clarify core skill update behavior for local template edits\",\n      \"completed_at\": \"2026-02-28T20:58:20.117Z\",\n      \"closed_reason\": \"Merged in PR #603. Implemented same-version template drift detection in skill update and explicit guidance to run 'kspec skill install-core' when local files differ despite matching version, including dry-run output. Added regression tests for drift guidance in tests/core-skill-update.test.ts. AC coverage confirmed for @core-skill-update ac-1, ac-2, ac-3; full regression suite passed via npm test.\",\n      \"origin\": \"observation_promotion\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"ref\": \"01KJGV65\",\n      \"slug\": null,\n      \"title\": \"Add integration test for config-aware init output messaging\",\n      \"completed_at\": \"2026-02-28T20:51:34.652Z\",\n      \"closed_reason\": \"Merged in PR #604. Added integration test coverage in tests/init-setup-integration.test.ts for config-aware init output messaging when running without --setup; verifies custom shadow directory (.specs) and branch (specs-meta) are shown in Next steps/Note output and guards against fallback to hardcoded defaults. AC coverage confirmed for @init-setup-integration ac-1 through ac-4 (trait ACs N/A).\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"ref\": \"01KJHAD8\",\n      \"slug\": null,\n      \"title\": \"Fix: Truncate oversized ACP prompt payloads\",\n      \"completed_at\": \"2026-02-28T19:01:41.319Z\",\n      \"closed_reason\": \"PR #590 reviewed and merged at head 690d0648\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"ref\": \"01KJJGJ1\",\n      \"slug\": null,\n      \"title\": \"Fix merge driver non-interactive flag and improve conflict resolution\",\n      \"completed_at\": \"2026-02-28T16:58:33.763Z\",\n      \"closed_reason\": \"Merged in PR #601. Fixed merge driver: (1) shadow.ts validates/fixes stale config missing --non-interactive, (2) TTY detection auto-enables non-interactive when stdin is not TTY, (3) non-interactive mode exits 0 even with conflicts per spec ac-10. All tests pass.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"ref\": \"01KJDQ19\",\n      \"slug\": null,\n      \"title\": \"CLI args should accept both kebab-case and underscore variants (e.g. depends-on and depends_on). Cur\",\n      \"completed_at\": \"2026-02-28T14:07:12.388Z\",\n      \"closed_reason\": \"Merged in PR #600. Implemented canonical arg-key normalization for batch args so kebab-case, camelCase, and underscore variants are accepted consistently in validation, required-arg checks, and argv generation. Added underscore regression tests in batch schema and batch exec engine coverage. Verified by full npm test (3550 passed) and green PR CI checks on commit b7b44fb4a11a5a4d655333b96a9e13368d95b9ed.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"ref\": \"01KJDQ11\",\n      \"slug\": null,\n      \"title\": \"Fix @observations slug ambiguity — kspec validate reports 6 errors for duplicate slug. Pre-existing \",\n      \"completed_at\": \"2026-02-28T13:53:13.698Z\",\n      \"closed_reason\": \"Merged in PR #599 (commit 5ee2254244a7c9aa718493418964a600869f4b97). Removed legacy /kspec:observations skill entry ambiguity by retaining canonical /kspec:observe in generated agent instructions; duplicate @observations reference errors resolved (References: OK). AC coverage N/A for this infra task (no spec_ref). Local regression: npm test passed (3548 passed, 0 failed).\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"recent_commits\": [\n    {\n      \"hash\": \"3eba720\",\n      \"full_hash\": \"3eba7201e29fc38355da7c3eb8b78be74888ad88\",\n      \"date\": \"2026-02-28T23:27:46.000Z\",\n      \"message\": \"fix: detach ralph session update listeners between iterations\",\n      \"author\": \"Jacob Chapel\",\n      \"task_refs\": [\n        \"01KJDQ1A\"\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"hash\": \"4c81ac5\",\n      \"full_hash\": \"4c81ac594ebc432e3e7114e003b0c374a5464704\",\n      \"date\": \"2026-02-28T23:19:12.000Z\",\n      \"message\": \"fix: use session-scoped ralph update attribution\",\n      \"author\": \"Jacob Chapel\",\n      \"task_refs\": [\n        \"01KJDQ1AF125H0FK29HE769R4P\"\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"hash\": \"3935ca8\",\n      \"full_hash\": \"3935ca808c131813871ec5a48e7550f9a239a5a1\",\n      \"date\": \"2026-02-28T23:14:04.000Z\",\n      \"message\": \"fix: prevent unhandled rejection on iteration timeout (Node.js 22) (#610)\",\n      \"author\": \"Jacob Chapel\",\n      \"task_refs\": [\n        \"01KJDQ17W\"\n","status":"completed"}